<title>USA: Trigen Energy Q1 shr drops.</title>
<headline>Trigen Energy Q1 shr drops.</headline>
<dateline>WHITE PLAINS, N.Y. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unaudited</p>
<p>						     Three Months Ended</p>
<p>								March 31,</p>
<p>							  1997	   1996</p>
<p>Revenues:</p>
<p>  Thermal energy				 $66,324	$69,605</p>
<p>  Electric energy				 14,088	 12,754</p>
<p>  Fees earned and other			  3,109	  3,860</p>
<p>    Total revenues				83,521	 86,219</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>  Fuel and consumables			  46,503	 47,808</p>
<p>  Production and operating		    14,182	 13,161</p>
<p>  Depreciation				     4,764	  4,193</p>
<p>  General and administrative		   9,495	  8,914</p>
<p>    Total operating expenses		  74,944	 74,076</p>
<p> Operating income				  8,577	 12,143</p>
<p> Interest expense net			  (4,056)	(4,250)</p>
<p> Minority interest				 (734)	  (801)</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		    3,787	  7,092</p>
<p> Income taxes					1,553	  2,911</p>
<p> Net income					  2,234	  4,181</p>
<p> Net income per share				.19	    .36</p>
<p> Average shares outstanding		   11,982	 11,469</p>
<p>		     (in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company, which develops and operates commercial district energy cogeneration systems,saud an unusually mild winter in the Northeast was partly responsible for the lower level of profits.</p>
<p>The company also cited the negative impact of legal fees of $1.3 million for the quarter, including litigation costs for an antitrust suit brought by Trigen against OG&amp;E in Oklahoma City.</p>
</text>
